Z||000000||Brad 86FieroGT||04-11-2001||12:20 AM||||Any one know of any companies that offer upgrades for TH-125 transmissions?||||reg||4
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-11-2001||03:38 AM||||I am going to be a wise guy, but Isuzu made some nice manual transmissions for the Fiero.  And then there's the Muncie 5spd . . .<P>Check out the Fierostore, they sell a shift kit for your transmission.  Here is a URL.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/pegasus/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/pegasus/index.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-11-2001||08:45 AM||||Twin Lakes Fiero will put in a T440 four speed automatic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||04-11-2001||09:21 AM||||A really good upgrade for a TH125 is to flush out all the old fluid and replace it with a Dexron III fluid. Especially good is a part synthetic ATF like the Quaker State Dexron.<P>This stuff gives you crisper shifts and is a lot more stable than the old formulation.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-11-2001||09:54 AM||||i've got a shift kit and AmsOil full synthetic she'll chirp second when the throttles cracked..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  the filter was EASY to change and the new valve plate is easy to install... just take a pressure washer to the engine bay before just to make sure you  don't get a bunch of nasty crap in the tranny and kill it...  and power braking it at the strip will kill the pump..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> or so i've heard... oh well... time for a rebuild anyway... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.northernautoparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.northernautoparts.com/</A>   -  for a shift kit.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">     <BR>www.engineered.net<BR>www.epdyno.com<BR>www.enthuzacar.com||||reg||1
