Z||000011||RedOktober||04-13-2001||03:06 AM||||Count me in as a lazy, stuck in traffic for 8 hrs a day, legs too tired to keep shifting, D for D'ataway driver, who can hold a big gulp and still have a smoke( at the same time even!). All I have to say is with the turbo... who cares to shift, but thats why most of us have more than one Fiero. Cheers. and Happy Holidays..<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cozmo||04-13-2001||08:16 AM||||A shift kit, designer tranny fluid and possible tranny swap for a 4T40/4T60 are all viable alternatives. I'll probably do all three when I do my engine conversion.<BR>As far as being a "lazy man" I 'fess up... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>At least I don't have to deal with that massive POS design they call a Fiero standard trans. and clutch....<BR>C02M0||||reg||1
Z||000013||trigger||04-13-2001||08:18 AM||||I've got a shift kit for sale.  I bought it from the Fiero Store opened it long enough to scare myself.  If you want it give me an e-mail at mumbles7@yahoo.com<BR><P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
